### Mundo Invest - API Test Collection
### Sequência de endpoints para testar a API

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

###############################################################################
### FLUXO 1: Criação de Cliente
###############################################################################

### 1. Criar cliente com patrimônio alto (>= 200.000 - prioridade alta)
POST {{baseUrl}}/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cliente_nome": "João Silva",
  "cliente_email": "joao.silva@example.com",
  "tipo_solicitacao": "Atualização cadastral",
  "valor_patrimonio": 250000
}

### 2. Criar cliente com patrimônio baixo (< 200.000 - prioridade normal)
POST {{baseUrl}}/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cliente_nome": "Maria Santos",
  "cliente_email": "maria.santos@example.com",
  "tipo_solicitacao": "Abertura de conta",
  "valor_patrimonio": 150000
}

### 3. Criar cliente com patrimônio no limite (= 200.000 - prioridade alta)
POST {{baseUrl}}/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cliente_nome": "Pedro Oliveira",
  "cliente_email": "pedro.oliveira@example.com",
  "tipo_solicitacao": "Resgate",
  "valor_patrimonio": 200000
}

### 4. Criar cliente com dados inválidos (email inválido)
POST {{baseUrl}}/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cliente_nome": "Carlos Lima",
  "cliente_email": "email-invalido",
  "tipo_solicitacao": "Atualização cadastral",
  "valor_patrimonio": 100000
}

### 5. Criar cliente com dados inválidos (campos obrigatórios faltando)
POST {{baseUrl}}/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cliente_nome": "Ana Costa",
  "tipo_solicitacao": "Abertura de conta"
}

###############################################################################
### FLUXO 2: Processamento de Webhook
###############################################################################

### 6. Processar webhook para cliente com patrimônio alto (prioridade alta)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_123",
  "card_id": "card_456",
  "cliente_email": "joao.silva@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T12:00:00Z"
}

### 7. Processar webhook para cliente com patrimônio baixo (prioridade normal)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_456",
  "card_id": "card_789",
  "cliente_email": "maria.santos@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T13:00:00Z"
}

### 8. Processar webhook para cliente com patrimônio no limite (prioridade alta)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_789",
  "card_id": "card_101",
  "cliente_email": "pedro.oliveira@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T14:00:00Z"
}

### 9. Processar webhook duplicado (idempotência - mesmo event_id do teste 6)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_123",
  "card_id": "card_456",
  "cliente_email": "joao.silva@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T12:00:00Z"
}

### 10. Processar webhook com cliente não encontrado
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_999",
  "card_id": "card_999",
  "cliente_email": "nao.existe@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T15:00:00Z"
}

### 11. Processar webhook com dados inválidos (event_id vazio)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "",
  "card_id": "card_111",
  "cliente_email": "joao.silva@example.com",
  "timestamp": "2026-05-27T16:00:00Z"
}

### 12. Processar webhook com dados inválidos (timestamp inválido)
POST {{baseUrl}}/webhooks/pipefy/card-updated
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "event_id": "evt_111",
  "card_id": "card_111",
  "cliente_email": "joao.silva@example.com",
  "timestamp": "timestamp-invalido"
}

###############################################################################
### FLUXO 3: Cenários Adicionais
###############################################################################

### 13. Criar cliente com nome curto (validação de comprimento mínimo)
POST {{baseUrl}}/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cliente_nome": "AB",
  "cliente_email": "ab@example.com",
  "tipo_solicitacao": "Atualização cadastral",
  "valor_patrimonio": 50000
}

### 14. Criar cliente com patrimônio negativo (validação)
POST {{baseUrl}}/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cliente_nome": "Teste Negativo",
  "cliente_email": "teste.negativo@example.com",
  "tipo_solicitacao": "Atualização cadastral",
  "valor_patrimonio": -1000
}

### 15. Criar cliente com patrimônio zero (validação)
POST {{baseUrl}}/clientes
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "cliente_nome": "Teste Zero",
  "cliente_email": "teste.zero@example.com",
  "tipo_solicitacao": "Atualização cadastral",
  "valor_patrimonio": 0
}

###############################################################################
### INSTRUÇÕES DE USO
###############################################################################
# 
# Este arquivo pode ser usado com:
# - VS Code (extensão REST Client)
# - IntelliJ IDEA (built-in HTTP Client)
# - Bruno (cliente HTTP open source)
# - Insomnia (importar como coleção)
#
# Para usar no VS Code:
# 1. Instale a extensão "REST Client" de Huachao Mao
# 2. Abra este arquivo
# 3. Clique em "Send Request" acima de cada requisição
#
# Para usar no terminal com curl:
# Copie cada requisição e execute no terminal, substituindo {{baseUrl}} por http://localhost:8080
#
# Exemplo:
# curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/clientes \
#   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
#   -d '{"cliente_nome": "João Silva", "cliente_email": "joao.silva@example.com", "tipo_solicitacao": "Atualização cadastral", "valor_patrimonio": 250000}'
#
###############################################################################
